msgid "SingleCopter and CoaxCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:10
#: 6f6a45fee99d4bc39ba6e083a0a7105b
msgid "SingleCopter with vertically mounted autopilot.  Image courtesy of \"droner\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:12
#: 892db171f87c473697b28f550e9a0b05
msgid "Single and Coax copters have one or two propellers to provide thrust and 2 to 4 individual flaps to provide roll, pitch and yaw control.  The difference between a SingleCopter and a CoaxCopter is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:14
#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:69
#: 37be2afa0205419ba0e018635f3abb66
#: 1da5b4f72b5a4d499f2bdb315498ac40
msgid "*SingleCopter*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:16
#: d581cfc865944ecd9da34cbe906c921d
msgid "has a single motor and 4 independent flaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:17
#: f2e0c4449f65489990a004b41e375fd0
msgid "the vehicle's yaw is controlled by adjusting all four fins to point slightly clockwise or counter-clockwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:19
#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:75
#: ac274deb65224a20ad95d92e8348042c
#: 930df8de71c14b0ea673e176ef81dfcf
msgid "*CoaxCopter*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:21
#: 4ec2447a0b5c4fc5b9e48ebca8226485
msgid "has two counter-rotating motors and at least 2 independent flaps (4 individual servos/flaps can be used but fins on opposite sides of the vehicle will move together)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:22
#: d46d2df806d443a6b872f07e9d357e4c
msgid "the vehicle's yaw is controlled by adjusting the speeds of the two motors.  I.e. speeding up the clockwise motor while slowing down the counter-clockwise motor will cause the vehicle to rotate counter-clockwise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:25
#: 009569428e234231b41d28d2bfe9ce47
msgid "Mounting and Connecting the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:30
#: 2dfd494fdc9a46c48f390b8d5af178af
msgid "By default the autopilot should be mounted similar to a \"plus\" quad.  The board should be horizontal with the white arrow pointing towards the forward flap. As with other vehicles the board should be placed close to the center of gravity of the vehicle. If it is more convenient to mount the autopilot pointing up, set :ref:`AHRS_ORIENTATION <AHRS_ORIENTATION>` to 25 (Pitch270)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/singlecopter-and-coaxcopter.rst:34
